WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.025
Open WebUI can support document and knowledge workflows where uploaded material is used as

00:00:05.025 --> 00:00:06.760
context for model responses.

00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:07.680
At a high level,

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:11.720
retrieval-augmented generation involves indexing or retrieving relevant content and

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:13.440
placing it into the model's context.

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:16.050
Embeddings help represent text for similarity search.

00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:18.145
This can make private documents more usable,

00:00:18.145 --> 00:00:20.800
but it also creates new data handling responsibilities.

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:23.590
Document sensitivity should be considered before upload.

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:27.650
Files may contain personal information, client data, business plans, credentials,

00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:30.940
internal procedures, regulated content, or proprietary research.

00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:33.960
Once uploaded, they may be stored, indexed, backed up, searched,

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:35.535
or reused in conversations.

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:38.410
Treat document features as part of a data management system,

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:39.960
not just a convenience button.

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:42.645
Source organization improves retrieval quality and review.

00:00:42.645 --> 00:00:45.870
Knowledge collections should have clear names, purpose, ownership,

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:47.212
and freshness expectations.

00:00:47.212 --> 00:00:49.715
Stale documents can produce outdated answers.

00:00:49.715 --> 00:00:52.990
Inaccurate retrieval can surface irrelevant or conflicting material.

00:00:52.990 --> 00:00:55.945
Retrieved content should be treated as evidence for the model to use,

00:00:55.945 --> 00:00:57.240
not unquestioned truth.

00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:58.830
Retention and cleanup matter.

00:00:58.830 --> 00:01:02.140
Decide how long uploaded documents should remain, who can access them,

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:05.420
how they are removed, and whether backups preserve them after deletion.

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:06.590
For important workflows,

00:01:06.590 --> 00:01:10.345
users should be able to trace an answer back to source material and understand whether the

00:01:10.345 --> 00:01:11.110
source is current.

00:01:11.110 --> 00:01:13.840
Retrieval is most valuable when it remains auditable.
